 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation: \"dov' è?\" is printed on two notes and kept as two words; Leporello's \"otto cento.\" is printed as two words (no hyphen across the barline), where the libretto has ottocento; Elvira sings \"e a me non torna ancor\" where the libretto has \"e se a me non torna ancor\", and \"cavare\" twice in the coda. Elvira's \"Chi è\" in the last bar (bar 108) begins the next recitative and is not in this piece's phrases. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S06) and the IPA was checked against Castel. Elvira sings her two quatrains twice with repeats of \"gli vo' cavar il cor\"; Giovanni's and Leporello's asides come between her lines. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
